flowchart TB
  accTitle: One monitoring connection, three views
  accDescr: The composition Wire connects Node Exporter's node-metrics Anchor, which provides the interface, to Prometheus's scrape-target Anchor, which requires it. A materializer writes the Node Exporter endpoint into Prometheus's scrape configuration. The runtime panel reads left to right from Prometheus, the HTTP client and consumer, to Node Exporter, the HTTP server and provider. The Wire connects provider to consumer; the HTTP request goes from consumer to provider.

  subgraph declaration["1. Declare the Wire in composition.yaml"]
    direction LR
    provides["DotInstance: node-exporter<br/>Anchor: node-metrics<br/>PROVIDES"]
    requires["DotInstance: prometheus<br/>Anchor: scrape-target<br/>REQUIRES"]
    provides -->|"Wire"| requires
  end

  subgraph configuration["2. Write the consumer configuration"]
    direction LR
    endpoint["Node Exporter endpoint<br/>host + port"]
    target["Prometheus configuration<br/>one scrape target"]
    endpoint -.->|"materializer writes"| target
  end

  subgraph runtime["3. Prometheus initiates the HTTP request"]
    direction LR
    prometheus["Prometheus<br/>HTTP client (consumer)"]
    exporter["Node Exporter<br/>HTTP server (provider)"]
    prometheus -->|"HTTP GET /metrics"| exporter
  end

  declaration ~~~ configuration
  configuration ~~~ runtime

  classDef declared fill:#e8f2f7,stroke:#2b6777,color:#17232d,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef configured fill:#fff7d6,stroke:#b7791f,color:#17232d,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef running fill:#eef6f3,stroke:#39826f,color:#17232d,stroke-width:1.5px;
  class provides,requires declared;
  class endpoint,target configured;
  class prometheus,exporter running;
